// N0 corpus row `impl-wider-than-trait` (plans/backlog/REFERENCES_AND_ORIGINS.md §8 N0;
// manifest tests/origins/corpus.tsv): an impl returning a borrow wider than its trait method's result origin (O7: an impl is checked against its trait method; the caller side of a `Dyn` call is `dyn-call-*`).
// Expected once decision 43's rules land: rejected in the impl: `other` is not within `self`.
_Pick :: trait(pick : (fn(self : &Self, other : &i32) -> &(i32, self)));
_P :: struct(v : i32);
impl(_P, _Pick(pick : (fn(self : &Self, other : &i32) -> &(i32, self))(other)));
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  p := _P(v : i32(1));
  o := i32(2);
  _ := p.pick(&o).*;
  ()
});
export(main);
